  "title": "fix: convention drift findings get nondeterministic file_id from HashMap iteration",
  "description": "From sutra/104 review. `comp_to_file` HashMap is built from `file_to_component` (also a HashMap) iteration, which is nondeterministic. Multiple files map to the same component, and HashMap::collect() keeps the last inserted value. Different runs attach the same drift finding to different files.\\n\\nFix: sort the iterator by path before collecting, or pick a deterministic representative.\\n\\nFile: src/health/drift.rs:94-99",
